WF-43 — Post-Consultation Handler

## Summary

- Inputs (canonical WF-01 envelope per data-contract-discipline Phase 1 §2.1): `phoneNumber` (E.164 string, top-level), `messageType` (enum: 'text' | 'interactive'), `messageContent` (string), `rawMessage` (object — for interactive payloads), `user.id` (integer), `user.status` (enum: 'consultation_closed'), `user.current_consultation_id` (integer or null), `user.slack_channel_id` (string — required for btn_done Slack notification).
- Outputs: Routes to WF-44 (feedback), WF-45 (rebook), WF-47 (unsubscribe); sends a thank-you (btn_done) via WF-50 + Slack notification via WF-51; or sends a Gemini-generated WhatsApp reply (per design.md §2.3 for WF-50 input contract and §2.4 for WF-51 input contract).
- State Transitions: none directly (downstream WFs may transition)
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-25 (Intent Classifier), WF-44 (Feedback Recorder), WF-45 (Rebook), WF-47 (Unsubscribe), WF-50 (Send WhatsApp), WF-51 (Send Slack Message — btn_done notification only)
- **Notes:**
  - TD-DRIFT-009 (WF-25 caller passes messageText instead of messageContent) is a known bug deferred to the post-Phase-1 bug-fix sprint.
  - **Gemini General Response halt-and-notify (2026-05-27 — TD-PGF-09 scope expansion):** Identical pattern to WF-23/WF-30/WF-31. HTTP node has `onError=continueErrorOutput`; on retries exhausted, error branch fans out to user apology (WF-50) + dual admin alerts (WF-51 consult + admin-commands), then `stopAndError` terminates execution. Consultation-closed users always have a consult Slack channel (Design Rule #10 — never archived) — both alerts fire. User-apology + admin-alert copy locked 2026-05-27T02:25:00Z. See revised Algorithm Step 13-23 for full chain.
  - **Call WF-25 envelope add-on (2026-05-27 — TD-PGF-05):** previously `workflowInputs.value` was empty (passthrough-via-trigger). Now explicit 6-field mapping per data-contract-discipline: phoneNumber, userId, messageText, userStatus, userName (`user.name`), slackChannelId (`user.slack_channel_id`). WF-25 reads these for its halt-and-notify alert template.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by another workflow (typically WF-01/WF-02 for a user in `consultation_closed`). Receives WF-01 canonical envelope.
Step 2: Check: Is messageType == "interactive" (a button reply)?
  - If YES → go to Step 3
  - If NO  → go to Step 8
Step 3: Check button_reply.id in order (cascade of IF gates):
  - IF rawMessage.interactive.button_reply.id == "btn_done"  → go to Step 5
  - ELSE IF rawMessage.interactive.button_reply.id == "btn_rebook" → go to Step 4
  - ELSE (btn_feedback or any other id) → go to Step 7
Step 4: Call WF-45 (Rebook) with phoneNumber, userId. End.
Step 5: Build canonical WF-50 payload (per design.md §2.3): { phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: "Thank you for choosing Chinmay Astro. We hope to see you again — just send REBOOK whenever you're ready.\n\nYou can also email chinmay_astro@gmail.com anytime if you need anything we can't help with here, or reply STOP if you'd prefer to unsubscribe." }; call WF-50.
Step 6: Build Slack notification payload (per design.md §2.4) — channelId = user.slack_channel_id; messageText = "✅ User tapped \"Done, thanks\" — conversation closed. Channel stays open for any future rebook."; call WF-51. No state change (user.status remains consultation_closed). End.
Step 7: Prompt for feedback — build canonical WF-50 payload (per design.md §2.3): { phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: "✍️ Thanks for choosing to share your feedback! Please type your thoughts about the consultation and send them — we appreciate every word!" }; call WF-50. End.
Step 8: Call WF-25 (Intent Classifier) with 6 fields per data-contract-discipline (TD-PGF-05, 2026-05-27): phoneNumber, userId (user.id), messageText (canonical envelope `messageContent` re-keyed for WF-25 input contract), userStatus (user.status), userName (user.name), slackChannelId (user.slack_channel_id) → returns intentResult. WF-25 may itself halt-and-notify on its own Gemini outage; that halt propagates here via executeWorkflow error semantics and on to WF-02.
Step 9: Check: intentResult == "stop_intent"?
  - If YES → call WF-47 (Unsubscribe) with phoneNumber, userId, userStatus. End.
  - If NO  → go to Step 10
Step 10: Check: intentResult == "rebook_intent"?
  - If YES → call WF-45 (Rebook) with phoneNumber, userId. End.
  - If NO  → go to Step 11
Step 11: Check: intentResult == "feedback_intent"?
  - If YES → call WF-44 (Feedback Recorder) with phoneNumber, userId, messageContent. End.
  - If NO  → go to Step 12
Step 12: Build Gemini prompt instructing a helpful, warm assistant for Chinmay's Vedic astrology consultation service on WhatsApp, with the user-stage cue "user has completed their consultation with Dr. Chinmay" and the email-callout cue "they can follow up here on WhatsApp or email chinmay_astro@gmail.com for anything else". Ask Gemini to weave both naturally into a brief 2-3 sentence reply. Append the user's messageContent.
Step 13: POST to Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash-lite) with temperature=0.3, maxOutputTokens=200, timeout=10s, retryOnFail=true, maxTries=3, onError=continueErrorOutput. On success: GOTO Step 14. On retries exhausted (error output): GOTO Step 16 (halt-and-notify).
Step 14: Extract reply text from candidates[0].content.parts[0].text; fallback = "Thank you for your message! For questions about our Vedic astrology consultation, feel free to ask."
Step 15: Call WF-50 (per design.md §2.3) with { phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: <reply> }. End.
Step 16: Build user apology WF-50 payload per §2.3 — { phoneNumber, messageType="text", messageContent="Sorry — we ran into a brief technical issue and couldn't process your message just now. Dr. Chinmay has been notified and will follow up with you shortly. We apologise for the inconvenience." }.
Step 17: Call WF-50 (apology). Continue to admin alert chain.
Step 18: Build admin alert text (Code) — translate userStatus to plain English (consultation_closed → "consultation completed"). Resolve userName. Construct General Response failure variant messageText. Emit { messageText }.
Step 19: Check `Has Consult Channel?` — is `user.slack_channel_id` non-empty (notEmpty unary)?
  - If YES → GOTO Step 20.
  - If NO → GOTO Step 22.
Step 20: Build consult alert payload — { channelId: `user.slack_channel_id`, messageText: `$('Build Admin Alert Text').item.json.messageText` }.
Step 21: Call WF-51 (consult-channel alert). GOTO Step 22.
Step 22: Build admin-commands alert payload — { channelId: "C0A5B0ZE81E", messageText: `$('Build Admin Alert Text').item.json.messageText` }.
Step 23: Call WF-51 (admin-commands alert). GOTO Step 24.
Step 24: stopAndError — terminate execution. End.
